# Line endings and binary classification.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Without it, every clone decides line endings from its own core.autocrlf, so
# the same file is text on one machine and something else on the next, and a
# checkout on Windows can produce a whole-file diff nobody edited. The index is
# currently LF throughout (verified with `git ls-files --eol`); this pins that
# so it stays true regardless of any individual machine's git config.
#
# NOTHING IS RENORMALISED BY ADDING THIS FILE. These rules apply as files are
# next written or checked out. Run `git add --renormalize .` deliberately, on a
# quiet tree, when you want the existing content converted.

# ── default ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `text=auto` lets git DETECT: content with NUL bytes is left binary and never
# EOL-converted. That auto-detection is load-bearing here and is the reason the
# source extensions below are not force-marked `text` — see the note further
# down about .mjs.
* text=auto

# ── source and config: text, normalised to LF in the repository ─────────────
# eol= is deliberately NOT set, so the working tree still follows the local
# core.autocrlf (currently `true` on this machine, i.e. CRLF on checkout).
# Forcing eol=lf here would mark every one of the ~880 CRLF working-tree files
# as modified on sight, which is exactly the phantom diff this file is meant to
# end.
*.js     text
*.jsx    text
*.cjs    text
*.json   text
*.css    text
*.md     text
*.yml    text
*.yaml   text
*.txt    text
*.svg    text
*.example text
.gitignore text
.gitattributes text

# ── .mjs IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT FROM THE LIST ABOVE ─────────────────────────
# Three tracked .mjs files contain a literal NUL byte, used as a field
# separator inside a composite-key template string:
#
#   scripts/audit-orphan-registrations.mjs
#   scripts/lib/legacy-source-manifest.mjs
#   scripts/rewrite-legacy-references.mjs
#
# git already classifies all three as binary (`git ls-files --eol` reports
# i/-text w/-text) and therefore leaves their bytes alone. Writing `*.mjs text`
# would OVERRIDE that detection and subject those three to EOL conversion —
# rewriting files whose exact bytes are currently being relied on. `* text=auto`
# above already covers the other ~219 .mjs files correctly.
#
# If the NUL bytes are ever replaced (U+241F renders the same intent and greps
# cleanly), these files become ordinary text and `*.mjs text` can be added.

# ── binary: never EOL-converted, never diffed as text ───────────────────────
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.xlsx   binary

# ── generated ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Collapsed in diffs and excluded from language stats; still tracked, still
# merged normally.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
